---
import Reveal from "../Reveal.astro";
import IteratorsLogo from "../icons/IteratorsLogo.astro";
import { links } from "../../site.ts";


const offers = [
  { title: "Kickoff", text: "We stand your project up on the template and shape the first modules around your domain, with your team in the room from day one." },
  { title: "Build", text: "We build the product on it, backend, web and mobile, alongside your people or as the whole team. You own every line and every decision." },
  { title: "Review", text: "A second pair of eyes on architecture, security and the parts of the template you changed, before they meet real traffic." },
  { title: "Support", text: "Upgrades from upstream, incidents and the awkward questions, answered by the people who wrote the code." },
];

---
<section class="m-section m-section--flush">
  <div class="m-container">
    <Reveal class="support-hero">
      <p class="m-eyebrow">Paid support and consulting</p>
      <p class="by"><span class="m-muted">by</span> <a href={links.iterators} rel="noopener" aria-label="Iterators"><IteratorsLogo height={26} /></a></p>
      <h1>Build on madrileño with the team that wrote it.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Iterators is a software consulting company. We've built products for founders and product teams for thirteen years, and madrileño is the part of that we could put in a repository. If you're starting on it, we can get you further than the docs alone.</p>
      <a class="m-button m-button--primary" href={links.iteratorsContact} rel="noopener">Schedule a call</a>
    </Reveal>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="m-section">
  <div class="m-container two-col">
    <Reveal>
      <p class="m-eyebrow">Why this template exists</p>
      <h2>We kept rebuilding the same backend.</h2>
    </Reveal>
    <Reveal>
      <p>Project after project, the first two months looked the same: sign-in, background jobs, events that can't be lost, flags, tracing. Work nobody is paying you to do twice.</p>
      <p>So we stopped rebuilding it. madrileño is that work in the open, on the same terms we use ourselves, and the <a href="/manifesto/">manifesto</a> is the reasoning behind it. Hiring us buys the part that doesn't fit in a repository: the judgement about what to keep, what to delete and what to build next.</p>
    </Reveal>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="m-section">
  <div class="m-container">
    <Reveal>
      <p class="m-eyebrow">How we help</p>
      <h2>Four ways in.</h2>
    </Reveal>
    <Reveal class="m-grid">
      {offers.map((o) => (
        <div class="m-card"><h3>{o.title}</h3><p>{o.text}</p></div>
      ))}
    </Reveal>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="m-section">
  <div class="m-container two-col">
    <Reveal>
      <p class="m-eyebrow">Track record</p>
      <h2>Thirteen years, hundreds of projects.</h2>
    </Reveal>
    <Reveal>
      <p>Fintech, healthtech, broadcasting, machine learning, HR. Founders raising a first round, and companies that already had a platform team and needed more hands on it.</p>
      <p>We've also built whole engineering teams for clients and handed them over, which is usually the harder half of the job.</p>
      <a class="m-button" href="https://www.iteratorshq.com/portfolio/" rel="noopener">See the portfolio</a>
    </Reveal>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="m-section">
  <div class="m-container two-col">
    <Reveal>
      <p class="m-eyebrow">Who this is for</p>
      <h2>Small teams with a deadline.</h2>
    </Reveal>
    <Reveal>
      <p>Founders and product teams who need a backend that holds up, without hiring a platform team to keep it that way.</p>
      <p>Tell us what you're building and where you're stuck. We answer quickly, and we say no when we're not the right people.</p>
      <a class="m-button m-button--primary" href={links.iteratorsContact} rel="noopener">Talk to Iterators</a>
    </Reveal>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  .support-hero { max-width: 46rem; padding-top: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 4rem); }
  .by { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .by a { display: inline-flex; color: var(--m-ink); }
  .by svg { display: block; }
  .lede { font-size: 1.2rem; }
  .two-col { display: grid; gap: 2rem 4rem; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr); align-items: start; }
  @media (max-width: 48rem) { .two-col { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
